ents","hybrid","nextjs","node","react","server-rendering","ssg","static","static-site-generator","universal","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":30029,"open_issues":3156,"watchers":136480,"default_branch":"canary","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls/61174","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61174","diff_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61174.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/61174.patch","merged_at":"2024-01-30T23:28:47Z"},"body":"### What\r\nCatch-all parallel slots were being incorrectly matched to the root of their segment. For example, `@foo/[...catchAll]/page` as a parallel route on `/page.tsx` should not match on `/`, but it should match on `/foo`, `/bar`, ...etc\r\n\r\n### Why\r\nThe catch-all route normalization logic doesn't treat optional catch-all routes differently from catch-all routes. The assumption was if any catch-all route was found, that it should match the path that shared its prefix.\r\n\r\n### How\r\nThis updates the normalization logic to handle optional-catchall as it was in the original implementation. For regular catch-all, we ensure that the catch-all base path (for `/[...slug]` that'd be `/`) isn't identical to the path we'd match it to.\r\n\r\nFixes #60613\r\nCloses NEXT-2243\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/61174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/61174/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":11648847657,"node_id":"CE_lADOBC3Cis58AQv_zwAAAAK2U08p","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/events/11648847657","actor":{"login":"ztanner","id":1939140,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzkxNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars